KG42.register("clusters-a683ef1da0d80adcd4242095",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v142-d-CL001","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","label":"Stackelberg internal pricing, consumption response, and coordination for the next period","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"Stackelberg internal pricing, consumption response, and coordination for the next period","market_meaning":"MGO selects internal prices using prosumer consumption responses, aggregate purchase and sale quantities, and external electricity prices. After broadcasting the prices, it receives each prosumer's selected consumption, forming sharing arrangements for the next period. The operator's profit objective, obligation to trade externally under imbalance, and server configuration are retained with the original chain; this candidate has not yet formed an optimization rule with closed mathematical and implementation interfaces.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","coordination","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The chains belong to M01 scheduling for the same microgrid, but the general model, initialization, implementation timing, and reported case have separate scopes of applicability. R008-C002/C003/C007 and their electricity-price values are limited to the original case and are not elevated to general price-adjustment laws or general parameters; versions of the price domain, consumption bounds, and forecast-quantity interfaces remain to be clarified.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Assembly follows the information links among price decisions, response aggregation, and consumption reporting, forming a candidate closed loop for a single arrangement for the next period. Participation rights, base transaction payments at given prices, and ex post deviation billing have independent conditions and outcomes and are assembled into separate clusters. The server provisions in R003 serve only as implementation context and do not justify adding dependencies.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Completes the ordering relationship between broadcasting internal prices and submitting selected consumption."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides price responses, aggregate purchase and sale quantities, and the timing of the final arrangement, connecting pricing to sharing quantities."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Specifies the recipient of selected consumption, the coordination objective, and operational responsibilities; the infrastructure provisions of the original chain remain retained."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Connects internal prices, consumption responses, and price publication, retaining the original conditions governing the direction of response."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides MGO price decisions, the profit objective, and selection among regions; initialization and case observations retain their respective scopes."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_p_s","v141-c-R008::x::x_p_b"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-ps","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-pb"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g03-E06"],"rationale":"Within the same M01, the internal prices selected by MGO are price inputs to consumption responses and aggregate trading quantities; the distinct roles of decision variables and local input parameters are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-Eb","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-Es","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g03-E06","v141-b-g03-E09"],"rationale":"Aggregate purchase and sale quantities enter MGO profit and the selection of surplus or deficit regions. This mapping points only to the uses of quantities in the existing R008 expressions and does not supply their missing local type references."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_p_s","v141-c-R008::x::x_p_b","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x002","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e019"],"rationale":"The source text explicitly states that MGO broadcasts the internal prices for the next period after obtaining them; the pricing result and coordination signal are different uses of prices for the same period."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g02-E04"],"rationale":"The two chains cover adjacent procedural scopes: broadcasting after optimization, and selecting and submitting consumption after the broadcast. Only the original sequence is assembled; no new requires or transitive scientific edges are inferred."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x001","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g02-E04"],"rationale":"R001 establishes the submission sequence, while R003 specifies that the submitted object is each prosumer's selected total consumption and that the recipient is MGO; this message is not relabeled as a net electricity purchase bid from buyers only."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e010"],"rationale":"The two chains reuse the conditional consumption-extremum relationship in source Eq. (2), serving signal response and quantity aggregation respectively; they are not counted as two independent response rules."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e014"],"rationale":"The coordinator's own profit objective and responsibility for grid transactions under imbalance receive corresponding explanations in the profit accounting of the pricing chain; profit terms cannot substitute for the still-missing graph objects for executing external transactions."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e019"],"rationale":"Both refer to the pricing function for internal buying and selling prices in M01; only a display entry point is selected, while the original chain nodes and their scopes remain unchanged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e020"],"rationale":"In the source text, optimization, pricing, and receipt of consumption are all undertaken by the MGO of the same microgrid; normalization of node presentation does not merge constraints on distinct responsibilities."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M003","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g02-E04"],"rationale":"Both occurrences represent the coordination signal for broadcasting internal prices for the next period and apply to the same process."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M004","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g02-E04"],"rationale":"Both occurrences represent the submission of selected consumption by all participating prosumers; the existing node identifiers are retained, and total consumption is not equated with net demand."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_p_s","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x002","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-ps"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e019"],"rationale":"The internal selling price for the same period serves respectively as an MGO decision, a broadcast signal, and a response input; each local variable or parameter object is retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M006","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_p_b","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x003","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-pb"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e019"],"rationale":"The internal buying price for the same period has three local roles: pricing decision, coordination signal, and clearing input; these are not rewritten as a single object."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M007","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-xn","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e015"],"rationale":"Both are consumption decisions for a period by the same M01 prosumer, used respectively for response and aggregation; this does not justify directly merging the general decision quantity with the selected value in R003."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M008","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-kn","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-t001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g03-E10"],"rationale":"Both are the preference parameter of the same prosumer in Eq. (2); retain the original records, with no assigned value in one occurrence and a positivity condition attached in the other."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M009","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-Eng","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-t002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e012"],"rationale":"Both are period-specific PV generation inputs in the same response model; this correspondence does not extend to asserting equality between forecast and actual generation."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M010","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-xmin","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-t005"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015"],"rationale":"Both occurrences reference the lower bound of the same prosumer's strategy set; linking the parameters does not fabricate a best response at the boundary."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M011","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-xmax","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-t006"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015"],"rationale":"Both occurrences reference the upper bound of the same prosumer's strategy set, and their respective local bindings remain retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M012","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-t003","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_s"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g02-E01"],"rationale":"The source text calibrates the general export electricity price in the reported case; alignment applies only to that case instance, and the R008 numerical value does not override the general scope of the R004 symbolic parameter."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M013","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-t004","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_b"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g02-E01"],"rationale":"The source text calibrates the general import electricity price in the reported case; the symbolic and case-specific numerical records are retained, without generalizing the value as fixed across all periods or regions."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M014","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e010"],"rationale":"Both occurrences transcribe the same Eq. (2), including the same branches and the premise excluding zero net energy; deduplication is for presentation only and does not endorse it as a complete best response covering all boundaries."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G001","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The response expression excludes zero net energy, and its extrema may not satisfy the upper and lower consumption bounds or the conditions of the corresponding buying or selling branch. The existing chain lacks a complete utility objective and optimal choices at boundaries or kinks, so the aggregation expression cannot unconditionally cover all feasible consumption.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-t005","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-t006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e015"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream must clarify the conditions of applicability concerning bounded consumption, zero net energy, and role preservation, and supply the objects required for a complete response; D does not independently add a clipping formula."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G002","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The strict ordering of buying and selling prices in the main text, the separately specified non-strict price bounds in the appendix, and the import-price upper bound carrying a prosumer index do not constitute the same confirmed feasible domain. Solving by region cannot currently be treated as directly satisfying all constraints in the main text.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C006","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g03-E07","v141-b-g03-E08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the price-upper-bound index and the scope of applicability of the strict price spread, clarify how the optimization domains in the main text and appendix correspond, and retain the original expressions until upstream revision."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G003","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The appendix text interchanges the buying and selling labels of E^b and E^s, whereas their definitions and summation sets correspond to buyers and sellers respectively. This cluster references quantities according to the existing formulas, retains the textual contradiction, and does not exchange objects or symbols.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-Eb","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-Es","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g03-E06"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the source page and have upstream confirm the nature of the label discrepancy; quantity definitions must not be silently exchanged when revising the explanation."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G004","category":"upstream_missing","description":"Forecasting, preference calibration, and role declarations before pricing have not been represented in corresponding frozen chains. Explicit instance interfaces are also missing between model generation and forecast generation, and between general consumption x_n and submitted selected consumption x_n^o; these cannot be merged merely because their symbols are similar.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-Eng","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x001","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e018","v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g02-E02","v141-b-g02-E03","v141-b-g03-E01"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Supplement the upstream representation of pricing-input declarations, explaining the instance relationships between forecast and model quantities, the fixed scope of role sets, and how selected consumption is transmitted."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G005","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R003 retains the obligation to trade externally under imbalance, but lacks graph representations of the corresponding imbalance conditions and grid-transaction actions. The R008 profit terms provide a financial interpretation and cannot be used to supply physical execution objects.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e014"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Have C supply conditions and representations of external transactions supported by sources, with any necessary ontology extensions proposed separately; there are currently no node proposals awaiting approval that can be referenced."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G006","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The expression for comparing regional optima, attainability of optima at open boundaries, tied outcomes, and empty buyer or seller sets remain unresolved. The two diagonal terms in appendix (29) use different external electricity prices; their relationship to the use of a single external electricity price in each region's profit also requires checking, and a globally unique equilibrium cannot be established on this basis.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E07","v141-b-g03-E08","v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E10","v141-b-g03-E11"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the regional objectives and Hessian, explain the conditions for the existence of solutions within each region and the semantics of selection across regions, and independently recheck uniqueness; do not rewrite the frozen Eq. (30)."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G007","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The R008 profit and region-partition expressions use aggregate purchase and sale quantities, but these quantities are absent from its local type references. The quantity interface with R002 can explain their uses but cannot substitute for complete bindings within C. R008-C004 contains an optimization problem, whereas C008 provides only a profit expression; neither is deleted as a duplicate constraint.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-Eb","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-Es","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g03-E09"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Have C specify the quantity references and local roles in the profit and region-partition expressions, retaining the distinction between optimization constraints and profit subexpressions."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G008","category":"unverified_source","description":"This cluster is assembled from candidate evidence permitted by the experiment; B remains UNREVIEWED and source_status is unverified, and no B source audit, independent C2 recheck, or Agent E review has been conducted.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g03-E06","v141-b-g03-E11"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the sources, conditions, and mathematical interpretations chain by chain; this round of assembly does not constitute endorsement of transcription accuracy or scientific validity."}]},"rule_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R004","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-221ff4096aa50456","COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","COMP-c556f6f82fb7db9e","KG31-36e0a27c810a788e","KG31-84de1f1af39d310b"]});
